# The image needs exactly what the Dockerfile copies; everything else is excluded up front.
# Not a size optimisation: the mock rig writes root-owned Postgres data under demo/ (b-pg, c-pg,
# d-pg), and a `docker build .` run as a normal user on Linux fails while merely STAT-ing them
# ("checking context: can't stat 'demo/b-pg'"). Excluding the tree means the walk never descends.
*
!package.json
!package-lock.json
!src/
# The Rust image build needs the crate and the COMMITTED UI it embeds at compile time
# (rust/src/web/assets.rs include_str!s ../../../src/web/dist/). Both target/ and .cargo-home/
# live under rust/ and are gigabytes, so they are re-excluded explicitly.
!rust/
rust/target/
rust/.cargo-home/
src/**/*.test.ts
src/web/ui/
